{"kind":"artifact","text":"docs/reference/mcp/status.md at f83d5cd52d7588abc78d716c157d53056cd36d12 on request/commitment-honesty.\n\nThe page explains the bounded orientation and why some categories accumulate — it lists the states that never discharge, so a reader understands why a capped list keeps growing. Both new statuses belong in that list, because neither released nor revoked is terminal.\n\nThat paragraph is also the one no gate watches. The docset surface gate checks tool schemas against their pages and caught the enum omission on work.md twice; nothing checks this prose against the fold at all. I found it only by grepping every file that mentions an existing status word after the gate had told me I was finished, which is why a gate covering one surface is worse than none in one particular way.\n\nIt now rests on cmd/gitseq-mcp and internal/statusview, the two packages whose behaviour it describes, rather than on the documentation-set commit it named before.","body":{"branch":"request/commitment-honesty","commit":"f83d5cd52d7588abc78d716c157d53056cd36d12","head":"f83d5cd52d7588abc78d716c157d53056cd36d12","path":"docs/reference/mcp/status.md"}}